    skos:definition "the root of the *Panax quinquefolium* of America, which fetches an enormous price in China, from its imaginary stimulating properties. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 184]"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Curated classification (group=grp_drugs_medicinal_botanicals): Named materia medica (castoreum, ginseng, cubebs, scammony, maidenhair, liquorice juice, quassia, cocculus indicus, serpentary, asafoetida, cantharides, hellebore, pipsissewa, ipecacuanha) left in the residual bin. Layer-1 observations: 14 rows, 1800–1829. Series: KEW_CUST 4 ×10; KEW_CUST 5 ×4. Units: Lbs. (Pounds) ×14. Top routes: Canada → England ×4; Canada → London ×3; Canada → Great Britain ×3; Holland → United Kingdom ×1."@en ;
